WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.550
Ahhhh!

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.520
It's Rob Lucci!

4
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.670
Then it's true.

5
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.100
They came here to kill Vegapunk,
just as he feared that they would.

6
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.230
Who the hell invited
you, Pigeon Guy?

7
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:15.510
You get outta here!

8
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.020
Go!

9
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.850
This is a Government island.

10
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.900
[HATTORI caws]

11
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.290
[gasps] Oh crap, you're right!

12
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.400
We're the ones who aren't
supposed to be here!

13
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:24.890
[CHOPPER] Ah!

14
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:25.730
Will you focus?

15
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.860
None of that matters!

16
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.460
Come on, Luffy!

17
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.590
We gotta get
to the upper level, now!

18
00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.100
[KAKU] The Straw Hats, huh?

19
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.940
Didn't know this place
had a pest problem.

20
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.560
Jewelry Bonney, too.

21
00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.760
But we can't do
anything yet, Lucci!

22
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.760
Remember, Straw Hat is
an Emperor of the Sea now,

23
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.370
We can't fight him without
permission from the top.

24
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:46.450
[STUSSY] He's right.

25
00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.440
The Four Emperors often
have powerful allies.

26
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.790
One little scuffle
could lead to a war.

27
00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.670
Send a report
to the Navy now.

28
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.550
Roger!

29
00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.800
I'm not sure we can avoid
a fight so easily.

30
00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.780
[gasps]

31
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.160
Gotta go, Jinbe!

32
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.250
Hold Bonney!

33
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.400
Huh?

34
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.190
[CHOPPER]
Luffy, what's the matter?

35
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.950
What happened?

36
00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.530
[CHOPPER gasps]

37
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.310
Wait, I know her!

38
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.310
It's that girl from before!

39
00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.320
Chopper! Help her, please!

40
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.350
[CHOPPER] I'm sorry, but.

41
00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.370
I think this is more Franky's
specialty than mine!

42
00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.870
[LUCCI]
This is Government business.

43
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.110
You would be wise
to stay out of it.

44
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.500
She fed us.

45
00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.510
She took care of us
when we came here,

46
00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.080
and that makes her a friend!

47
00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:53.340
Ah,

48
00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.650
<b>Marine Headquarters</b>

49
00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.700
The straw hats
are on Egghead?

50
00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.060
Why, dammit?

51
00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.420
See this?

52
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.920
You give people an inch and they
give you nothing but a headache.

53
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.120
He must have figured out that
CP0 was there to kill them.

54
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.490
That's not a good sign.

55
00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:46.480
Yes, sir.

56
00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.090
That's likely why they had
to use S-Bear to teleport inside.

57
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.950
And what they did
is declare war.

58
00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.060
I wish they'd had the common
sense to contact...

59
00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:57.860
Me first!

60
00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:59.580
Those arrogant brats.

61
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:04.210
If Vegapunk has the Straw Hats on his side,
this could be a real disaster.

62
00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.080
Who knows how many good
Marines we could lose.

63
00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:09.630
Where's Kizaru?

64
00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.450
He's on his way
to Egghead right now.

65
00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:16.000
He was already en route
in service of a different mission.

66
00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:20.260
Tell Lucci to avoid any further
action until backup arrives.

67
00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.290
[growls]

68
00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.110
[MARINE OFFICERS] Sir!

69
00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.550
No matter what happens,
we cannot let him fight Straw Hat!

70
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.250
<b>Egghead
New World</b>

71
00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.480
[PYTHAGORAS] Intruder alert!

72
00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:32.390
Evacuate immediately!

73
00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.240
I repeat, evacuate
immediately!

74
00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.170
<b>The Strongest Form of Humanity</b>

75
00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.290
[laughs]

76
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.150
Hey!

77
00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.740
Yoo-hoo!

78
00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.350
Pigeon guy, get over here!

79
00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.750
Let's fight some more!

80
00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:57.180
[LUCCI] Still playing games, even
when your life is on the line?

81
00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.280
I'm starting to get annoyed.

82
00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:04.450
N-No!

83
00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:11.950
Eantackle.

84
00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.830
[yells]

85
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.260
[laughs]

86
00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.180
[yelps]

87
00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.320
[LUCCI]
Don't get cocky, Straw Hat.

88
00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.250
I've gotten stronger,
just like you have.

89
00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:39.650
<b>Cat-Cat Fruit: Leopard
Awakened Form</b>

90
00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:39.330
All the better to eat
prey like you alive.

91
00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.030
Wait, something's different!

92
00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.640
[USOPP] He definitely didn't
look like that before!

93
00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.240
[KAKU] Stop, Lucci!

94
00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.130
We don't have
authorization for this!

95
00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.510
[SHAKA] His speed is incredible,
but so is his control!

96
00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:03.710
It's rare that an awakened zoan user
can maintain their state of mind.

97
00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.260
[roars]

98
00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.140
[LUFFY laughs]

99
00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:28.240
It's rare that an...

100
00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:34.280
[CITIZENS screaming]

101
00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:37.300
Aaaaaaah!

102
00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.700
Please, think
of the position you're in!

103
00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.130
The Government will hunt
you down for this!

104
00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.960
[LUFFY laughing, yelping]

105
00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.440
Shaka!

106
00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:51.670
What happened?

107
00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.550
Did the white-haired
warrior appear?

108
00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.260
Oh my god, real Vegapunk!

109
00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.690
How in the hell did he
get up here so fast?

110
00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:00.490
Remarkable!

111
00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.170
Tell me more!

112
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.890
I must know everything
about this transformation!

113
00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.720
What is that form?

114
00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.100
Well, it's new, so we
don't know much, either,

115
00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:10.920
but it's a Gum-Gum
thing, right?

116
00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.770
That's a Devil
Fruit Encyclopedia,

117
00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.090
There is no mention
of a Gum-Gum Fruit.

118
00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.260
This must be something else!

119
00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:23.170
Huh?

120
00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:26.370
Wait, are you saying it's
a different devil fruit?

121
00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.780
If that's true, then why does
he say Gum-Gum all the time?

122
00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.290
[VEGAPUNK] He's so beautiful.

123
00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:39.650
There is a figure from
the ancient past.

124
00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.050
One with the same form
your captain has now!

125
00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:46.910
A god from the old texts!

126
00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.850
A god?

127
00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:50.260
I'm sorry, Luffy?

128
00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:51.880
Stupid incarnate, Luffy?

129
00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.790
Yes. The Warrior of Liberation.

130
00:07:57.170 --> 00:08:01.590
He who plays the fool
and brings smiles to all.

131
00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.820
There's no mistaking him.

132
00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:07.770
He is the Sun God! Nika!

133
00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:13.060
[laughs]

134
00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:12.120
Nika?

135
00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:13.710
I've never heard of him.

136
00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.120
That's no surprise.

137
00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.980
The World Government
erased his name from history.

138
00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:24.180
But as long as people yearn for the Warrior
of Liberation, he will never truly disappear!

139
00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:28.110
For it is desire that brings
forth everything in this world!

140
00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:32.610
Take for example the devil fruits
and all their power!

141
00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:34.140
[gasps]

142
00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.390
You can see it, can't you?

143
00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:42.300
[VEGAPUNK] Each devil fruit is a possibility
for evolution that someone desires!

144
00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:40.770
[laughs]

145
00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.920
I wish I could do this.

146
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.780
I wish I could do that.

147
00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:49.720
All of the powers represent
potential futures of humanity!

148
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:54.480
But these fantastic possibilities are
not a natural part of this world,

149
00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:58.420
so the mother of nature,
the sea, rejects them!

150
00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.150
Therefore, you might say...

151
00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:10.410
[VEGAPUNK] Those who have powers
live in different realities.

152
00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:14.020
Realities someone
dreamed up!

153
00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:21.250
[VEGAPUNK]
That is my hypothesis!

154
00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:26.650
One where god's
existence is irrelevant!

155
00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:30.550
What an interesting world,
wouldn't you say?

156
00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:35.970
[LUFFY laughing]

157
00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.630
[SENTOMARU] Do those idiots know
where they're fighting?

158
00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:40.520
This isn't a playground!

159
00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.530
Not for pirates,
and not for CP0, either!

160
00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:45.980
<b>Sentomaru
Captain of Marine Headquarters' Science Corps</b>

161
00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:47.280
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL A ringing]

162
00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:49.120
Why are you bothering
me on my day off?

163
00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.100
[VEGAPUNK] Why did you take
so long to answer?

164
00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:52.390
Whatever!

165
00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:53.560
I'm here, aren't I?

166
00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.650
So what's the plan, Punk?

167
00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:59.320
Cipher Pol is our ally,
and the pirates are the enemy, right?

168
00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:02.990
Do you want me to just
back up CP0, or what?

169
00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.520
[VEGAPUNK]
Quite the opposite, I'm afraid.

170
00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:10.220
CP0 is here to assassinate me,
so I need your help to escape.

171
00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.970
[VEGAPUNK] Don't get caught
up in the details.

172
00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.200
Just keep them away!

173
00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.310
I can't do that!

174
00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.550
Do you know what
they do to traitors?

175
00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.370
You're right.

176
00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.850
My apologies.

177
00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.450
But let me ask you this.

178
00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:24.610
Sentomaru?

179
00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.810
Can't you do this one
teensy favor for me?

180
00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.320
The man who saved
you from poverty?

181
00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.700
All those years ago?

182
00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:35.810
Wow!

183
00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:36.920
No pressure, huh?

184
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:38.800
Huh?!

185
00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.150
Is he going to attack us?

186
00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:52.760
[KAKU] Three seraphim.
I'm not looking forward to this.

187
00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:55.340
S-Bear!

188
00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.830
Thin out their numbers!

189
00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.070
S-Bear!

190
00:10:59.150 --> 00:10:59.990
Don't move!

191
00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:02.700
We can't beat them.

192
00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:03.530
Not like this.

193
00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.360
Go, S-Bear!

194
00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:06.290
Take out CP0.

195
00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.750
They're the enemy!

196
00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.250
[BOTH gasp]

197
00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:13.960
Retreat!

198
00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:18.880
[AGENTS scream]

199
00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.630
We need a new plan, and fast.

200
00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:26.660
[KAKU] No kidding.

201
00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:31.680
So the issue is that Sentomaru outranks
the Authority Chips we're carrying?

202
00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:32.610
That's right.

203
00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:34.850
The system of control
is a hierarchy.

204
00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:37.230
If someone who's higher
ranked gives an order,

205
00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:39.380
that's the order
the seraphim will follow.

206
00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:43.010
The highest on the authority
chain are the Five Elders.

207
00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.200
[STUSSI] The second highest
is Dr. Vegapunk.

208
00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.320
The third is Sentomaru.

209
00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.530
<b>Authority Chip</b>

210
00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:56.300
And Authority Chip holders
like us are the fourth.

211
00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:01.650
No matter what we do, Sentomaru's
commands will always be prioritized!

212
00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:06.180
[KAKU] Then why don't we make a call
to the Five Elders and have them take control?

213
00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:07.600
It doesn't work that way.

214
00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:11.150
Pacifistas have to receive
their commands directly.

215
00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:13.820
They won't react
to a Transponder Snail,

216
00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:16.140
Even if it's
the Five Elders calling!

217
00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.030
[KAKU] Then what are we
supposed to do?

218
00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:22.360
The seraphim are valuable
Government property,

219
00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.730
We can't just destroy them!

220
00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:24.900
Darn it, Lucci.

221
00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:27.000
You really didn't
think this through!

222
00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.760
[growls]

223
00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:31.580
Grrrr! Grrrr! Grrrr! Grrrr!

224
00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.220
[LUCCI yells]

225
00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:39.800
Grrrr! Grrrr! Grrrr!

226
00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:43.880
[laughs]

227
00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:40.710
Hahahaha!

228
00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:46.660
You ready?

229
00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:50.470
Gum-Gum...

230
00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:52.990
Mole Pistol!

231
00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.690
Time to do this!

232
00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:04.820
First, S-Snake, guide Straw Hat
and his friends to the Vacuum Rocket!

233
00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:07.550
They need to make it
to the Frontier Dome!

234
00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:11.630
S-Hawk, S-Shark!
Hold CP0 back!

235
00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:15.040
Chopper, do those children
look familiar to you?

236
00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:18.930
[yells]

237
00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:20.300
Apart from the black wings and the flames,
they all look like former Warlords of the sea.

238
00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.420
You're right!

239
00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.830
There's no way
that's a coincidence!

240
00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:26.020
[laughs]

241
00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:26.680
[JINBE] The Government must have
made clones out of us.

242
00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.190
Hey!

243
00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:29.560
Axe Guy!

244
00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:32.400
[LUFFY laughs]

245
00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:34.630
[AGENTS yelling]

246
00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.820
It's been a while, old buddy!

247
00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.050
Psh!

248
00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:37.500
Straw Hat!

249
00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:41.220
Current circumstances aside,
you and I are enemies.

250
00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:42.660
And I have a name!

251
00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.280
So, what?

252
00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.640
You're helping Punk escape?

253
00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.110
Do I have that right?

254
00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.000
Uh-huh.

255
00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:49.390
I like his apple head.

256
00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:50.440
And he asked.

257
00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.480
Well, that doesn't exactly
fill me with confidence,

258
00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.900
but I suppose you
are an Emperor now.

259
00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:05.640
[SENTOMARU gasps]

260
00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:07.000
Hand pistol.

261
00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.260
[gasps] Black sky!

262
00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.610
[LUCCI] That takes care
of their commander.

263
00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:20.750
[GIRL A screams]

264
00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.150
Seraphim!

265
00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.420
You follow our orders now.

266
00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:25.760
[LUFFY] I'm sorry!

267
00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.860
I distracted you
and now you're dead!

268
00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:29.790
[SENTOMARU] Idiot.

269
00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.780
You didn't distract me.

270
00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:34.710
I saw that hit coming.

271
00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:41.250
Ugh! Damn it!

272
00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.200
I was so sure...

273
00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.220
I blocked in time.

274
00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.350
[LUCCI growls]

275
00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.310
Hurry up and die.

276
00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.400
I can't take control until
you're unconscious.

277
00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:16.070
[LUFFY grunting]

278
00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.500
[laughs]

279
00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:41.310
[LUFFY yells]

280
00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:49.390
[LUCCI] I'm sure you thought
you had a fine strategy,

281
00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.510
overriding our orders
to the seraphim,

282
00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:50.420
but all you did was put a nail

283
00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:55.510
in your own coffin!

284
00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:41.390
Lucci.

285
00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:45.200
[chuckles]

286
00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:49.500
Chance!

287
00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:48.990
[yelping]

288
00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:51.540
Hurry, Luffy!

289
00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:55.970
If we want to save this girl's life, then we
have to get to Vegapunk's lab immediately!

290
00:16:56.490 --> 00:17:01.090
[LUFFY] I mean, it's not like I
don't want to, but, uh...

291
00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:58.550
[screams]

292
00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:03.560
[laughing]

293
00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.890
[LUFFY] I can't stop spinning!

294
00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:16.430
Whoa!

295
00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.380
You really can't stop spinning!

296
00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:31.490
Hurry!

297
00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:40.740
Whoa!

298
00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:55.820
[AGENTS gasping]

299
00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.910
[AGENTS yell]

300
00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:03.520
Is there nothing we can do
to stop these things?

301
00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.940
We're losing men
to our own weapons!

302
00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:09.610
[STUSSY] I shudder to imagine how strong
they'll be once they grow up.

303
00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:11.750
[FRANKY] Hey, Vegapunk!

304
00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:14.350
What's wrong?

305
00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.250
[FRANKY] Tell me the truth.

306
00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:17.810
What is that power?

307
00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:20.770
And what the hell is that
Jinbe thing doin' with it?

308
00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:23.610
'Cause that looks like
the Swim-Swim Fruit to me!

309
00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:25.270
[NAMI]
What's the Swim-Swim Fruit?

310
00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:26.750
It's his.

311
00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:31.030
My hard-boiled brother from another
mother, señor Pink, has that power.

312
00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:33.300
I'd recognize it anywhere.

313
00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:41.830
[FRANKY] But it's impossible
for there to be two

314
00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:44.730
of the same devil fruit,
so that means my bro

315
00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:45.900
must have died!

316
00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:50.090
Ah! My poor bro!

317
00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:51.890
So you would think.

318
00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:53.850
But he's not dead.

319
00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:56.180
He's just being held
in Impel Down.

320
00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:58.550
Hold up.

321
00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:02.380
Does that mean you found
a way to duplicate devil fruits?

322
00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:07.160
[VEGAPUNK] Well,
some devil fruits can be copied.

323
00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:13.410
But it only works
with zoan-types.

324
00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:14.580
Hm.

325
00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:21.590
Though the less said about Caesar's
SMILE experiments, the better.

326
00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:22.350
Yeah.

327
00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:23.960
He can go straight to hell.

328
00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:30.320
The SMILEs offer a high
risk and low success rate.

329
00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.760
They only work one
time out of ten.

330
00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:36.420
And those who aren't granted power
never stop smiling or laughing.

331
00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:39.210
They can't even mourn
for their lost loved ones.

332
00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:40.080
It's sick.

333
00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:41.260
[FRANKY] Caesar.

334
00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:45.330
Just hearin' his name again
makes me wanna blow chunks.

335
00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:50.720
Oh, aberrations such as
those notwithstanding,

336
00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:53.190
I have not given up.

337
00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:58.510
If we had enough funding, and enough time,
we could replicate any devil fruit

338
00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.290
in the world!

339
00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:01.190
[laughs]

340
00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:01.930
Oh.

341
00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.230
[VEGAPUNK]
I'm not sure if they'll Awaken.

342
00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.150
Hm.

343
00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:15.310
I've tried to recreate logia
powers, but I've had no luck.

344
00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:16.730
And yet...

345
00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:23.300
For a Paramythia Fruit, I need only acquire
the Bloodline Elements of its owner.

346
00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:28.450
Then, I can synthesize a special compound
which, when administered, confers the...

347
00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:30.760
devil fruit power
to another person.

348
00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:36.710
[VEGAPUNK] Observe!

349
00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:40.380
That's the fluid you see flowing
through the seraphim's arms!

350
00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.280
The Green Blood!

351
00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:46.760
Hold up!

352
00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:48.660
You made a new
kind of blood?

353
00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:51.990
[VEGAPUNK chuckles]

354
00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:52.730
Love-Love...

355
00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:56.260
Beam!

356
00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:06.300
[VEGAPUNK] I believe
that seraphim represent

357
00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:11.140
the pinnacle of modern
scientific possibility!

358
00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.820
Ursa Shock!

359
00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.330
Beans!

360
00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:20.200
[AGENTS scream]

361
00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:25.820
[VEGAPUNK] Do you know what
that makes them?

362
00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:30.180
The strongest form
of humanity in history!

363
00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.330
Is that why the Government
got rid of them?

364
00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:38.310
Why the hell would you even make something
stronger than a Warlord, you psychopath?

365
00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:39.480
They're Navy weapons.

366
00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:41.120
Killing machines.

367
00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.000
Yes.

368
00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:45.130
And sooner or later,
they'll be aiming for us.

369
00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:57.520
[CITIZEN B]
Hold on, Sentomaru!

370
00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:00.260
[SENTOMARU] Stay back!

371
00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.530
This isn't over yet!

372
00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:08.080
[CITIZENS scream]

373
00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:16.500
[BOTH screma]

374
00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:18.150
[CITIZEN C]
Sentomaru, please stay safe!

375
00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:23.700
Now, where did that little
friend of yours run off to?

376
00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:25.380
I don't know!

377
00:22:26.140 --> 00:22:27.650
And he's not my friend!

378
00:22:28.090 --> 00:22:29.260
What a shame.

379
00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:31.360
Guess you're all alone, traitor.

380
00:22:33.770 --> 00:22:34.570
Huh.

381
00:22:57.940 --> 00:22:59.100
Yeah.

382
00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:50.150
A...

383
00:24:20.530 --> 00:24:22.850
I'm... gone.

384
00:24:27.710 --> 00:24:28.510
Focus!

385
00:24:34.930 --> 00:24:39.650
[LUCCI]
When did he get so powerful?

386
00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.270
[LUCCI] Damn it.

387
00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:49.830
[LUCCI]
I'm losing consciousness!

388
00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:51.780
[laughing]

389
00:24:56.700 --> 00:24:58.320
[CHOPPER gasps]

390
00:25:00.970 --> 00:25:02.620
Follow me! Quickly!

391
00:25:10.900 --> 00:25:14.660
[S-SNAKE] I said, hurry!

392
00:25:17.290 --> 00:25:20.350
This is no time to be dragging
your feet, you fools.

393
00:25:21.110 --> 00:25:23.050
The Vacuum Rocket
is right there.

394
00:25:23.660 --> 00:25:24.980
Now get on!

395
00:25:26.550 --> 00:25:27.860
Why, thank you!

396
00:25:27.940 --> 00:25:30.880
You know, you're much
kinder than the real Hancock!

397
00:25:31.300 --> 00:25:32.380
We owe you one!

398
00:25:32.460 --> 00:25:33.930
Much obliged!

399
00:25:34.010 --> 00:25:35.210
[S-SNAKE]
What? D-Don't be absurd!

400
00:25:35.580 --> 00:25:37.640
I-I'm just following
orders, all right?

401
00:25:38.230 --> 00:25:40.110
[JINBE laughs]

402
00:25:41.780 --> 00:25:44.700
[alarm sounding]

403
00:25:43.350 --> 00:25:46.190
[ANNOUNCER B] Vacuum Rocket
departing in one minute.

404
00:25:48.740 --> 00:25:49.720
Hurry up!

405
00:25:52.170 --> 00:25:55.480
What do I do?

406
00:25:55.960 --> 00:25:56.980
[ANNOUNCER B] Attention.

407
00:25:57.060 --> 00:25:59.980
Please take caution while
boarding the rocket.

408
00:26:00.060 --> 00:26:00.860
[SENTOMARU] Straw Hat!

409
00:26:03.450 --> 00:26:04.450
Go!

410
00:26:04.530 --> 00:26:05.820
And take care of Punk!

411
00:26:06.250 --> 00:26:07.410
You hear me?

412
00:26:10.040 --> 00:26:10.720
Okay!

413
00:26:10.720 --> 00:26:11.470
Leave it to me!

414
00:26:14.530 --> 00:26:15.230
[SENTOMARU] No!

415
00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:16.800
You're going the wrong way!

416
00:26:19.340 --> 00:26:22.580
[ANNOUNCER B] Caution. Doors closing
in ten seconds.

417
00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:35.900
We're gonna get
him off this island.

418
00:26:37.980 --> 00:26:39.150
No matter what.

419
00:26:39.230 --> 00:26:40.170
I promise!

420
00:26:51.300 --> 00:26:52.400
[ANNOUNCER B]
Doors closing.

421
00:26:59.220 --> 00:27:00.910
[ANNOUNCER B]
Prepare to launch.

422
00:27:07.340 --> 00:27:08.140
Woooah!

423
00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:12.630
[CHOPPER, JINBE scream]

424
00:27:13.920 --> 00:27:18.320
It's certainly
something right!

425
00:27:19.930 --> 00:27:22.310
[LUFFY groans]

426
00:27:20.410 --> 00:27:21.710
[BONNEY]
What happened to Vegapunk?

427
00:27:28.920 --> 00:27:29.840
It's Luffy.

428
00:27:29.920 --> 00:27:30.950
He's just tired!

429
00:27:31.030 --> 00:27:32.630
I'll give you the details later!

430
00:27:32.580 --> 00:27:34.010
How long was I passed out?

431
00:27:34.530 --> 00:27:35.740
[CHOPPER grunts]

432
00:27:35.740 --> 00:27:38.100
[CHOPPER] Okay, maybe I'll
get used to it.

433
00:27:39.380 --> 00:27:39.980
[BONNEY] Please shut up!

434
00:27:39.980 --> 00:27:41.040
[LUFFY] Easy does it.

435
00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:42.800
[BONNEY]
You shut up, too, grandpa!

436
00:27:42.880 --> 00:27:47.440
Go back to normal already!

437
00:27:44.330 --> 00:27:47.500
[CHOPPER, BONNEY scream]

438
00:27:47.440 --> 00:27:49.040
[ANNOUNCER B]
Departing Fabriophase.

439
00:27:49.120 --> 00:27:51.340
Entering Labophase.

440
00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:59.980
[ANNOUNCER B]
Transit duration: 32 seconds.

441
00:27:59.910 --> 00:28:03.870
<b>Inside the Lab</b>

442
00:28:01.690 --> 00:28:02.840
You have arrived.

443
00:28:02.920 --> 00:28:03.620
[BONNEY] Already?

444
00:28:04.090 --> 00:28:06.720
[ANNOUNCER B] All subsequent
rockets are canceled.

445
00:28:06.800 --> 00:28:08.490
[ANNOUNCER A]
Labophase under lockdown.

446
00:28:08.570 --> 00:28:10.990
Frontier Dome security
system engaged.

447
00:28:12.440 --> 00:28:13.900
Hostile intruder alert.

448
00:28:15.020 --> 00:28:20.100
All researchers, evacuate to the factory
immediately and seal all entry points.

449
00:28:26.990 --> 00:28:28.990
Well, I will say
this for the man.

450
00:28:31.300 --> 00:28:33.860
He was a faithful
bodyguard to Vegapunk.

451
00:28:34.860 --> 00:28:36.590
Until his dying breath.

452
00:28:37.100 --> 00:28:38.400
Such a waste.

453
00:28:38.950 --> 00:28:41.220
Didn't have to end
like this, Sentomaru.

454
00:28:41.300 --> 00:28:45.400
Need I remind you, our orders are to wait
for the Navy before making a move.

455
00:28:45.480 --> 00:28:50.310
They can twiddle their thumbs all they
like, but I won't wait for Vegapunk to escape.

456
00:28:47.540 --> 00:28:51.000
<b>Lab</b>

457
00:28:51.190 --> 00:28:53.590
What do they even stand
to gain from killing you?

458
00:28:53.590 --> 00:28:56.380
You're the smartest man in the world,
and you're on their side.

459
00:28:56.380 --> 00:28:59.490
If they do this, it'll be
a huge loss for them.

460
00:28:59.570 --> 00:29:00.930
Well, I think so.

461
00:29:01.010 --> 00:29:04.780
But it appears that the higher-ups
have a different perspective.

462
00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:10.220
I certainly made inventions that have
been beneficial to the World Government.

463
00:29:10.240 --> 00:29:14.160
Innovations in navigation
technology using sea prism stones.

464
00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:16.600
Cyborg animal modifications.

465
00:29:17.780 --> 00:29:21.670
Not to mention my research on devil
fruits that's unlocked their secrets.

466
00:29:21.750 --> 00:29:25.110
Or my creation of human
weapons with the pacifistas.

467
00:29:26.100 --> 00:29:29.520
And now, I've completed
the seraphim as well.

468
00:29:30.600 --> 00:29:35.070
Now imagine if you thought I might turn
that frightful intelligence against you.

469
00:29:35.150 --> 00:29:36.590
What would you do?

470
00:29:36.670 --> 00:29:39.600
In that case,
there's no choice.

471
00:29:39.680 --> 00:29:40.470
Hm?

472
00:29:41.490 --> 00:29:43.540
I said, I will not!

473
00:29:43.620 --> 00:29:45.780
For the record,
I never planned to revolt.

474
00:29:45.860 --> 00:29:48.400
I still need my research
funding, after all.

475
00:29:48.750 --> 00:29:52.330
But the powers that be decided
I was trouble, and that was that.

476
00:29:52.970 --> 00:29:56.380
Alas, life gives you lemons,
government tries to kill you for them.

477
00:29:56.460 --> 00:29:59.160
That is not how the expression
goes, and you know it!

478
00:29:59.240 --> 00:30:03.720
Just when I faced this quandary,
an Emperor and his crew appeared before me.

479
00:30:03.800 --> 00:30:06.550
Fate brought us together,
don't you think?

480
00:30:07.630 --> 00:30:08.130
Hold it!

481
00:30:08.130 --> 00:30:09.680
You mean you want
to join our crew?

482
00:30:09.680 --> 00:30:11.360
Welcome aboard, crewmate!

483
00:30:11.750 --> 00:30:12.550
Super!

484
00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:17.080
Which of my babies do
you want to see first?

485
00:30:17.160 --> 00:30:18.540
The Sunny?

486
00:30:18.620 --> 00:30:20.070
General Franky?

487
00:30:20.890 --> 00:30:21.530
What?

488
00:30:21.530 --> 00:30:23.200
So we have to take him?

489
00:30:23.280 --> 00:30:24.640
Well, this sucks.

490
00:30:25.170 --> 00:30:26.460
Don't you worry, Nami!

491
00:30:26.830 --> 00:30:28.590
I'm on bodyguard duty.

492
00:30:28.670 --> 00:30:30.390
Oh my, what a gentleman.

493
00:30:30.470 --> 00:30:33.020
Thank you, I feel
much safer now.

494
00:30:33.100 --> 00:30:33.750
What?

495
00:30:33.750 --> 00:30:36.120
Shut up and unlock these
shitty shoes already!

496
00:30:36.200 --> 00:30:37.690
I wasn't talking to you!

497
00:30:38.440 --> 00:30:39.220
Oh no!

498
00:30:39.300 --> 00:30:40.050
Atlas!

499
00:30:40.130 --> 00:30:41.100
This is serious!

500
00:30:41.180 --> 00:30:42.590
She's not moving at all!

501
00:30:42.980 --> 00:30:44.960
Don't worry, we'll save you!

502
00:30:45.040 --> 00:30:46.870
Ready a repair
session immediately!

503
00:30:46.950 --> 00:30:48.420
Patient incoming!

504
00:30:48.500 --> 00:30:50.230
Thank you for bringing her in.

505
00:30:50.310 --> 00:30:52.020
You can leave the rest to us.

506
00:30:52.420 --> 00:30:53.890
Of course, good luck!

507
00:30:53.970 --> 00:30:55.300
Hey, screws for brains!

508
00:30:55.380 --> 00:30:56.920
Where the hell is Vegapunk?

509
00:30:57.900 --> 00:30:59.960
I know he's in here
somewhere.

510
00:31:00.040 --> 00:31:01.530
Tell me now!

511
00:31:01.610 --> 00:31:02.860
Bonney, stop it!

512
00:31:03.300 --> 00:31:04.980
You need to calm down!

513
00:31:07.750 --> 00:31:08.800
Wait a sec!

514
00:31:09.240 --> 00:31:10.240
Is this his lab?

515
00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:11.360
Wow!

516
00:31:12.510 --> 00:31:13.290
So cool!

517
00:31:13.290 --> 00:31:15.990
Are you seeing this, Buddy?

518
00:31:17.210 --> 00:31:19.020
That ancient bastard!

519
00:31:19.590 --> 00:31:21.230
I'm gonna make him pay!

520
00:31:25.320 --> 00:31:26.150
Bonney!

521
00:31:26.600 --> 00:31:28.130
Wait, where are you going?

522
00:31:32.070 --> 00:31:36.130
I told Vegapunk to turn my father
back to normal, and what did he do?

523
00:31:37.170 --> 00:31:38.960
He sicked bugs on me!

524
00:31:43.290 --> 00:31:45.090
I'm going to Bury him for this!

525
00:31:45.170 --> 00:31:47.780
I don't think the bugs
were his fault, though.

526
00:31:49.510 --> 00:31:50.380
Bonney, wait!

527
00:31:50.460 --> 00:31:51.990
We need to stick together!

528
00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:07.910
<b>Fabriophase</b>

529
00:32:08.220 --> 00:32:10.740
Our authority chips are
finally back in effect.

530
00:32:10.820 --> 00:32:13.140
The seraphim follow
our orders now.

531
00:32:13.880 --> 00:32:15.870
Who's ready
for a little revenge?

532
00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.510
I took down one
of the satellites.

533
00:32:20.060 --> 00:32:22.570
Including Vegapunk himself,
there are six more.

534
00:32:22.650 --> 00:32:24.390
This might not be easy.

535
00:32:24.470 --> 00:32:26.820
That's assuming we
can even get to them.

536
00:32:27.290 --> 00:32:31.290
Trust me, that defense
system is nothing to scoff at.

537
00:32:32.660 --> 00:32:33.420
Tch.

538
00:32:33.500 --> 00:32:36.270
We'll see how long it
lasts against our forces.

539
00:32:36.710 --> 00:32:38.190
Lock down the island.

540
00:32:38.270 --> 00:32:40.500
Destroy every last
ship you can find.

541
00:32:41.310 --> 00:32:43.660
No one escapes
Egghead on our watch!

542
00:32:53.480 --> 00:32:54.310
Huh.

543
00:32:55.620 --> 00:32:58.050
The Straw Hats are
protecting Vegapunk.

544
00:32:58.130 --> 00:32:59.640
How nice of them.

545
00:33:00.210 --> 00:33:03.240
Well, I'm sure
they'll be a big help.

546
00:33:05.820 --> 00:33:06.840
Too bad.

547
00:33:06.920 --> 00:33:08.490
They still won't escape.

548
00:33:12.020 --> 00:33:15.320
They're in for one hell
of a surprise, after all.

549
00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:18.140
Alright.

550
00:33:18.220 --> 00:33:20.790
Proceed according
to plan, boys.

551
00:33:20.870 --> 00:33:23.500
Send every last
ship we have...

552
00:33:25.420 --> 00:33:27.480
...to Egghead Island.
